<article class="env-definition" id="04PX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04PX">Definition <span data-tag="04PX">29.27.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $T \subset X$ be a connected component. The <em>canonical scheme structure on $T$</em> is the unique scheme structure on $T$ such that the closed immersion $T \to X$ is flat, see Lemma <a href="/tag/04PW" data-tag="04PW">29.27.1</a>. </p>
</article>